                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Thomas Thorp, 93 St Martin's Lane London,
                     Catalogue (November 1932), no. 678, priced at £60.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">Rev. Arno Clemens
                        Gaebelein</persName> (1861-1945) of Stony Brook, New York. This was the last
                     known provenance according to the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great
                     Britain (1964), and it was likewise listed as untraced in the supplement
                     (1987). The manuscript descended to Rev. Gabelein's son, <persName role="fmo"
                        >Rev. Frank Ely Gaebelein</persName> (1899-1983). It is not known what
                     happened to the manuscript after his ownership. Compare Schoenberg Database of
                     Manuscripts <ref target="https://sdbm.library.upenn.edu/manuscripts/2624"
                        >SDBM_MS_2624</ref>.</provenance>
